# path: /v1/images/edits
# base-url: https://api.meta.ai   (export META_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai ; the path above carries /v1)
# content-type: json
# model: muse-image-1.0
# verified: https://dev.meta.ai/docs/image-generation + https://dev.meta.ai/docs/api-reference/images/schemas (2026-10-28):
#   JSON body is Meta-specific: "images" = 1..10 items, each {"image_url": <public URL or base64 data URL>} or
#   {"file_id": ...}; the OpenAI SDK sends multipart "image" instead. The first image is the cutout, the rest are
#   the style refs from refs/*.png ({{REF_IMAGE_ITEMS}}, max 9). response_format b64_json (default), output_format
#   png|webp|jpeg (default webp). Reply: {"created", "data":[{"b64_json"}], "output_format", "background":"opaque",
#   "usage":{...}}. Price $0.01/image. Unknown top-level fields -> 400. mask / input_fidelity -> 400.
# unverified: "background" is documented as always "opaque" -> the transparent cutout background is probably NOT
#   preserved; the pipeline may need to re-cut the stylized output with SAM (sam-cutout on the result).
# changed 2026-10-28 (T10, live run 1): the prompt names the refs' look (bold even outline, flat crayon fills) and asks
#   to keep the character recognisable; the old one got thin sketchy lines. Mirrors core/meta Prompts.STYLIZE.
# changed 2026-10-28 (live run 4, runs/2026-10-28T07-46-08Z.json): child drawings came back almost unchanged (their
#   own strokes and saturated colours, Spark 0.15-0.55, 0/4 passed); the prompt now says a drawing must be redrawn
#   from scratch in the refs' soft palette, keeping each part's colour. Same day: "sticker" made Muse draw flat
#   digital fills with a die-cut white border and grey shadow (Spark still low, the matte kept the shadow ring), so
#   the word is gone and the prompt asks for the refs' fine crayon texture and no border.
#   Scratch runs on the 4 drawings: old prompt 0/4 first try (run 2026-10-28T07-46-08Z), "sticker" wording 0/4,
#   this wording 1/4 (drawing_car_2 0.907; the ladybug looks on-style but Spark still rates its red/black low).
# unverified: reasoning_strength "low" is faster (single pass); "high" (default) self-refines. Try both on Day 1.
{
  "model": "muse-image-1.0",
  "prompt": "The first image is a child's character: a photo of a toy or a child's own drawing. Either way, redraw the whole character from scratch in exactly the style of the reference images that follow, as if the same illustrator drew it; do not keep the original's strokes, scribbles or marker colours. Copy the references' bold, even outline (the same line weight and colour everywhere), their soft light palette, their flat crayon colour fills with the same fine crayon texture, and their simple friendly shapes with few details. Keep the character's identity so the child recognises it: the same silhouette, pose and features, and the same colour for each part in the references' softer tones. One character only, centred on a plain pure white background with wide margins, no border, no text, no shadow.",
  "images": [
    { "image_url": "data:{{INPUT_MIME}};base64,{{INPUT_B64}}" }{{REF_IMAGE_ITEMS}}
  ],
  "n": 1,
  "response_format": "b64_json",
  "output_format": "png",
  "reasoning_strength": "low"
}
